\subsection{Problem Formulation}
\label{sec:formulation}

We consider a \textbf{Vision-Language-Action (VLA)} policy $\pi(a_t \mid o_t, l)$ that maps a visual observation $o_t$ and a language instruction $l$ to a 7-DOF action $a_t$ (delta end-effector pose) at each timestep $t$. The policy is parameterized by a large pretrained vision-language model fine-tuned on robot demonstration data. We evaluate performance along two complementary axes. \textbf{Task Success Rate (TSR)} measures the fraction of episodes in which the robot completes the instructed task:
\begin{equation}
